Close #116

CSS Anchor Positioning needs Chrome/Edge 125+, Safari 26+, or Firefox 147+. Anywhere older `anchor()` is silently ignored and bindable markers have no way to find their marker, so labels collapse into a corner. On an older iOS that's *every* browser — Chrome, Edge and Firefox on iOS all use WebKit — so there's no "use another browser" workaround.

cobe already computes each marker's screen position every frame for the invisible anchor `<div>`. This publishes the same values as CSS custom properties, so a two-property fallback is enough:

```css
.marker-label {
  position-anchor: --cobe-sf;
  bottom: anchor(top);
  left: anchor(center);
  translate: -50% 0;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}

@supports not (anchor-name: --x) {
  .marker-label {
    left: var(--cobe-sf-x);
    bottom: calc(100% - var(--cobe-sf-y));
  }
}
```

New variables: `--cobe-{id}-x` / `-y` and `--cobe-arc-{id}-x` / `-y`, as percentages. No API or type changes.

### Notes

**Set on the canvas's parent element, not `:root`.** The values are per-instance, so on `:root` two globes sharing a marker id would send each other's labels to the wrong marker. It also keeps #120 working: coordinates change every frame, so putting them in the shared `<style>` tag would make its skip-write check always miss and swap a document-level stylesheet every frame. Labels inherit the variables from that element, which is also the containing block the percentages are relative to.

**Chromium rendering is unchanged.** The fallback only overrides `left` / `bottom` inside `@supports`, and the new variables are inert unless a stylesheet reads them.

The site was hiding labels with `display: none` where anchor positioning is missing; that's replaced with the real fallback, so the showcases, the playground and `/ip` render there now.

### Test plan

- [x] `pnpm build`
- [x] `pnpm --filter cobe-site build`
- [x] Chromium: no visual diff against `main`
- [x] iOS Safari (real device): labels track markers, fade is smooth
- [ ] Firefox desktop

