Currently Elasticsearch adapter supports IN queries, specifically implemented through the ```RexCall```  SEARCH → Sarg → terms query chain. The core logic is located in ```PredicateAnalyzer.java``` L193-195:

```
case INTERNAL:
  switch (call.getKind()) {
  case SEARCH:
    return canBeTranslatedToTermsQuery(call);
  }
```

This pr just add test cases for it.

The Workshop floor had three broken behaviors: the background video was clipped to a single section instead of filling the viewport, board previews rendered with a solid opaque canvas (breaking the paper-doll float effect), and boards had no reordering capability.

## Background video — full viewport

Moved `<video>` out of `.workshop-floor` and into the page root as a `position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: -1` element, covering the entire screen frame. Panel backgrounds reduced from ~93% to ~80% opacity so the video bleeds through.

## Paper-doll canvas

Added `.board-preview-grid--paper-doll` CSS modifier applied to all floor grid cards:

```css
.board-preview-grid--paper-doll .board-preview-grid__canvas {
  background: transparent;
  border: none;
  box-shadow: none;
}
.board-preview-grid--paper-doll .board-preview-grid__canvas::before,
.board-preview-grid--paper-doll .board-preview-grid__canvas::after { display: none; }
.board-preview-grid--paper-doll .board-preview-grid__legend { display: none; }
```

Board component PNGs now float over the background video with no coloured box behind them.

## Drag-to-reorder boards

- Added `sortOrder?: number` to `WorkshopBoardPayload`; `sortBoards` prefers it over timestamp.
- Added `reorderBoards(orderedIds[])` to `useWorkshopBoards` — persists new `sortOrder` values via Firestore (`setDoc merge`) for authenticated users and localStorage for guests. Boards absent from the ID list are preserved and appended.
- Board cards are `draggable` with `--dragging` / `--drop-target` modifier classes and reorder errors surface in the page error state.
